#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
gdrive-od — Google Drive "Files On-Demand" for Linux (KDE/Dolphin), built on rclone.

  * Every file in Drive shows up locally. Files not stored on disk are tiny
    placeholders named  "<name>.gdcloud".
  * Double-click a placeholder -> it downloads and opens.
  * Right-click -> Google Drive -> "Make available offline" / "Free up space".
  * Folders can be marked "always keep offline" (new files arrive downloaded).
  * Google Docs/Sheets/Slides become .gdoc/.gsheet/.gslides links that open in the
    browser profile configured for that account.
  * Two-way sync: local edits, new files, renames/moves and deletes go up; remote
    changes come down. Deletes go to the Drive trash / local trash (recoverable).
  * Near-instant: the daemon sees local changes through inotify and Drive changes
    through the Drive Changes API, and syncs only the affected folders. A full
    reconciliation runs at start and every `full_sync_interval` as a safety net.
  * Dolphin "Tags" column shows  Offline / Online only / Google file.

Commands:
  gdrive-od setup-desktop          install MIME types, Dolphin menu, systemd unit
  gdrive-od add-account NAME --email ADDRESS   connect a Google account (sign-in, config, service)
  gdrive-od sync [ACCOUNT...]      run one full sync now (all accounts if none given)
  gdrive-od daemon ACCOUNT         live sync (systemd service); SIGUSR1 = full sync now
  gdrive-od pin PATH...            make files/folders available offline
  gdrive-od unpin PATH...          free up space (back to online-only)
  gdrive-od open PATH              open a placeholder or Google file link
  gdrive-od web PATH               open the item in Drive web (right profile)
  gdrive-od status PATH...         show sync state
  gdrive-od reconnect [ACCOUNT...] sign in to Google again (expired/revoked token)
  gdrive-od backup pause|resume|now [ACCOUNT...]   control this PC's backup
"""
